{"id":"U11","title":"The Health Risks of Social Isolation","titleZh":"社交孤立的健康风险","paras":[{"id":"U11-P1","sentences":[{"id":"U11-P1-S1","hard":true,"text":"Social isolation poses more health risks than obesity or smoking 15 cigarettes a day, according to research published by Brigham Young University."},{"id":"U11-P1-S2","hard":false,"text":"The implication is that loneliness is a huge, if silent, risk factor."}],"zh":"根据杨百翰大学发表的研究，社交孤立带来的健康风险比肥胖或每天吸15支烟还要大。这意味着孤独是一个巨大的、尽管是沉默的风险因素。"},{"id":"U11-P2","sentences":[{"id":"U11-P2-S1","hard":false,"text":"Loneliness affects physical health in two ways."},{"id":"U11-P2-S2","hard":true,"text":"First, it produces stress hormones that can lead to many health problems."},{"id":"U11-P2-S3","hard":false,"text":"Second, people who live alone are less likely to go to the doctor appointments, to exercise or to eat a healthy diet."}],"zh":"孤独以两种方式影响身体健康。首先，它产生压力荷尔蒙，可能导致许多健康问题。其次，独居的人不太可能去看医生、锻炼或保持健康饮食。"},{"id":"U11-P3","sentences":[{"id":"U11-P3-S1","hard":true,"text":"Public health experts in many countries are debating how to address widespread loneliness in our society."},{"id":"U11-P3-S2","hard":false,"text":"Last year Britain even appointed a minister for loneliness."},{"id":"U11-P3-S3","hard":false,"text":"\"Loneliness touches almost every one of us at some point,\" its minister for loneliness Baroness Barran said."},{"id":"U11-P3-S4","hard":false,"text":"\"It can lead to very serious health consequences for individuals who become isolated and disconnected.\""}],"zh":"许多国家的公共卫生专家正在讨论如何解决我们社会中普遍存在的孤独问题。去年，英国甚至任命了一位孤独事务大臣。\"孤独几乎会在某个时刻触及我们每个人，\"其孤独事务大臣巴伦尼斯·巴伦说。\"它可能导致变得孤立和与社会脱节的人面临非常严重的健康后果。\""},{"id":"U11-P4","sentences":[{"id":"U11-P4-S1","hard":false,"text":"Barran started a \"Let's Talk Loneliness\" campaign that sparked difficult conversations across Britain."},{"id":"U11-P4-S2","hard":true,"text":"He is now supporting \"friendly benches\", which are public seating areas where people are encouraged to go and chat with one another."},{"id":"U11-P4-S3","hard":false,"text":"The minister is also pushing to stop public transportation from being cut in ways that leave people isolated."}],"zh":"巴伦发起了一场\"让我们聊聊孤独\"的运动，在英国各地引发了艰难的对话。他现在正在支持\"友好长椅\"，这是一些公共区域，人们被鼓励去那里相互聊天。这位大臣还在推动阻止公共交通以导致人们孤立的方式被削减。"},{"id":"U11-P5","sentences":[{"id":"U11-P5-S1","hard":false,"text":"More than one-fifth of adults in both the United States and Britain said in a 2018 survey that they often or always feel lonely."},{"id":"U11-P5-S2","hard":true,"text":"More than half of American adults are unmarried, and researchers have found that even among those who are married, 30% of relationships are severely strained."},{"id":"U11-P5-S3","hard":false,"text":"A quarter of Americans now live alone, and as the song says, one is the loneliest number."}],"zh":"2018年的一项调查显示，美国和英国都有超过五分之一的成年人表示他们经常或总是感到孤独。超过一半的美国成年人未婚，研究人员发现，即使在已婚者中，30%的关系也严重紧张。现在四分之一的美国人独居，正如歌中所唱，\"一\"是最孤独的数字。"}],"words":[{"id":"U11-W01","lemma":"isolation","surface":"isolation","pos":"n.","zh":"孤立; 隔离; 独处","sent":"U11-P1-S1","phrases":[{"en":"social isolation","zh":"社交孤立"},{"en":"in isolation","zh":"孤立地"}]},{"id":"U11-W02","lemma":"pose","surface":"poses","pos":"v.","zh":"造成; 引起; 提出; 摆姿势","sent":"U11-P1-S1","phrases":[{"en":"pose a risk","zh":"造成风险"},{"en":"pose a threat","zh":"构成威胁"}]},{"id":"U11-W03","lemma":"obesity","surface":"obesity","pos":"n.","zh":"肥胖; 肥胖症","sent":"U11-P1-S1","phrases":[{"en":"childhood obesity","zh":"儿童肥胖"}]},{"id":"U11-W04","lemma":"cigarette","surface":"cigarettes","pos":"n.","zh":"香烟","sent":"U11-P1-S1","phrases":[{"en":"smoke cigarettes","zh":"吸烟"},{"en":"a pack of cigarettes","zh":"一包香烟"}]},{"id":"U11-W05","lemma":"implication","surface":"implication","pos":"n.","zh":"含义; 暗示; 影响","sent":"U11-P1-S2","phrases":[{"en":"by implication","zh":"含蓄地"},{"en":"have implications for","zh":"对...有影响"}]},{"id":"U11-W06","lemma":"loneliness","surface":"loneliness","pos":"n.","zh":"孤独; 寂寞","sent":"U11-P1-S2","phrases":[{"en":"feel loneliness","zh":"感到孤独"}]},{"id":"U11-W07","lemma":"silent","surface":"silent","pos":"adj.","zh":"沉默的; 无声的","sent":"U11-P1-S2","phrases":[{"en":"silent risk","zh":"沉默的风险"},{"en":"remain silent","zh":"保持沉默"}]},{"id":"U11-W08","lemma":"affect","surface":"affects","pos":"v.","zh":"影响; 感染","sent":"U11-P2-S1","phrases":[{"en":"affect health","zh":"影响健康"},{"en":"negatively affect","zh":"负面影响"}]},{"id":"U11-W09","lemma":"physical","surface":"physical","pos":"adj.","zh":"身体的; 物理的; 物质的","sent":"U11-P2-S1","phrases":[{"en":"physical health","zh":"身体健康"},{"en":"physical exercise","zh":"体育锻炼"}]},{"id":"U11-W10","lemma":"produce","surface":"produces","pos":"v.","zh":"产生; 生产; 制造","sent":"U11-P2-S2","phrases":[{"en":"produce stress hormones","zh":"产生压力荷尔蒙"}]},{"id":"U11-W11","lemma":"stress","surface":"stress","pos":"n. / v.","zh":"n. 压力; 紧张 v. 强调; 使紧张","sent":"U11-P2-S2","phrases":[{"en":"stress hormones","zh":"压力荷尔蒙"},{"en":"under stress","zh":"在压力下"}]},{"id":"U11-W12","lemma":"hormone","surface":"hormones","pos":"n.","zh":"荷尔蒙; 激素","sent":"U11-P2-S2","phrases":[{"en":"stress hormones","zh":"压力荷尔蒙"}]},{"id":"U11-W13","lemma":"lead to","surface":"lead to","pos":"phr. v.","zh":"导致; 通向","sent":"U11-P2-S2","phrases":[{"en":"lead to problems","zh":"导致问题"}]},{"id":"U11-W14","lemma":"appointment","surface":"appointments","pos":"n.","zh":"预约; 约会; 任命","sent":"U11-P2-S3","phrases":[{"en":"doctor appointments","zh":"看医生"},{"en":"make an appointment","zh":"预约"}]},{"id":"U11-W15","lemma":"expert","surface":"experts","pos":"n.","zh":"专家; 行家","sent":"U11-P3-S1","phrases":[{"en":"public health experts","zh":"公共卫生专家"}]},{"id":"U11-W16","lemma":"debate","surface":"debating","pos":"v. / n.","zh":"v. 讨论; 辩论 n. 辩论; 讨论","sent":"U11-P3-S1","phrases":[{"en":"debate how to","zh":"讨论如何..."},{"en":"under debate","zh":"在讨论中"}]},{"id":"U11-W17","lemma":"address","surface":"address","pos":"v. / n.","zh":"v. 解决; 处理; 演讲 n. 地址; 演讲","sent":"U11-P3-S1","phrases":[{"en":"address a problem","zh":"解决问题"},{"en":"address the issue","zh":"处理问题"}]},{"id":"U11-W18","lemma":"widespread","surface":"widespread","pos":"adj.","zh":"广泛的; 普遍的","sent":"U11-P3-S1","phrases":[{"en":"widespread loneliness","zh":"普遍存在的孤独"}]},{"id":"U11-W19","lemma":"appoint","surface":"appointed","pos":"v.","zh":"任命; 委派; 约定","sent":"U11-P3-S2","phrases":[{"en":"appoint a minister","zh":"任命大臣"},{"en":"be appointed as","zh":"被任命为..."}]},{"id":"U11-W20","lemma":"minister","surface":"minister","pos":"n.","zh":"大臣; 部长; 牧师","sent":"U11-P3-S2","phrases":[{"en":"minister for loneliness","zh":"孤独事务大臣"}]},{"id":"U11-W21","lemma":"point","surface":"point","pos":"n. / v.","zh":"n. 时刻; 点; 观点 v. 指向","sent":"U11-P2-S3","phrases":[{"en":"at some point","zh":"在某个时刻"},{"en":"make a point","zh":"表明观点"}]},{"id":"U11-W22","lemma":"consequence","surface":"consequences","pos":"n.","zh":"后果; 结果","sent":"U11-P3-S4","phrases":[{"en":"serious consequences","zh":"严重后果"},{"en":"as a consequence","zh":"因此"}]},{"id":"U11-W23","lemma":"disconnected","surface":"disconnected","pos":"adj.","zh":"脱节的; 断开的; 孤立的","sent":"U11-P3-S4","phrases":[{"en":"become disconnected","zh":"变得脱节"}]},{"id":"U11-W24","lemma":"campaign","surface":"campaign","pos":"n. / v.","zh":"n. 运动; 活动 v. 参加运动; 发起活动","sent":"U11-P4-S1","phrases":[{"en":"start a campaign","zh":"发起一场运动"},{"en":"election campaign","zh":"竞选活动"}]},{"id":"U11-W25","lemma":"spark","surface":"sparked","pos":"v. / n.","zh":"v. 引发; 触发 n. 火花; 火花","sent":"U11-P4-S1","phrases":[{"en":"spark conversations","zh":"引发对话"},{"en":"spark interest","zh":"激发兴趣"}]},{"id":"U11-W26","lemma":"conversation","surface":"conversations","pos":"n.","zh":"对话; 交谈","sent":"U11-P4-S1","phrases":[{"en":"have a conversation","zh":"进行对话"},{"en":"difficult conversations","zh":"艰难的对话"}]},{"id":"U11-W27","lemma":"support","surface":"supporting","pos":"v. / n.","zh":"v. 支持; 支撑 n. 支持; 支撑","sent":"U11-P4-S2","phrases":[{"en":"support a cause","zh":"支持一项事业"}]},{"id":"U11-W28","lemma":"bench","surface":"benches","pos":"n.","zh":"长椅; 长凳","sent":"U11-P4-S2","ph